nic ideas  Jesus emerges as a Transcendent being  who manifests himself in terms like the  light of the world and the bread of life  it also contains many long monologues  that do not appear in the other Gospels  with this Jesus we are far removed from  the very human down to earth figure who  inhabits the gospel of Mark  but there are other first century  sources about Jesus one very important  source is the historian Josephus he was  born around 37 A.D just a few years  after the crucifixion into a Jewish  Priestly family in Jerusalem  30 years later when the first Jewish war  against the Romans began he was pressed  into Service as an officer leading a  regiment of Jewish resistance Fighters  while fighting in Galilee he was  defeated by the Roman Legions under the  command of General Vespasian but he  saved his life by foretelling that this  General Would One Day become emperor  sure enough in July of 69 A.D the  spacious Legions pronounced him  imperator  Josephus was released and eventually  followed the emperor to Rome where he  wrote a book about the Jewish War  he later published another more detailed  book about Jewish history  even though Josephus is not particularly  interested in early Christians his books  are incredibly valuable for  understanding the world of first century  Galilee and Judea he even writes about  John the Baptist as well as Jesus  another important source is the Jewish  mishnah  the mishna is a record of debates  between rabbis about the application of  the Torah the Jewish law in everyday  life  although the book was first compiled  around 200 A.D many scholars believe  that some of its case studies go back to  the first century  the mishna is important because it  touches on many topics that Jesus and  the Pharisees debate in the gospels such  as the observance of the Sabbath ritual  Purity marriage laws and the role of  women in society  two supplements to the mishnah the  bharata and the tosafta even include  references to yeshu 